* CSS `@keyframes typing` gradually expands the text width, creating the “typing” effect.
* The `blink` animation adds a cursor‑like blinking bar at the end of the text.
* The animation runs once (5 seconds by default) and stops with the full text displayed.

Feel free to adjust the `animation` duration, colors, or add a delay by editing the CSS inside the `<style>` block. If you need any further tweaks—different speed, color, or a start‑delay—just let me know!
